### Overview

This indicator tracks the extent of tree canopy cover in the region, as measured by the National Forest Inventory (NFI). Tree canopy cover is an important aspect of urban greening, biodiversity and climate resilience. The NFI source [dataset](https://data-forestry.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/d62fd97664a64596844b9834c1737e46_0/explore) is filtered by the "Woodland" category and clipped to the boundary of the West of England to provide a regional measure of the area covered by woodland.


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![](index_files/figure-html/RI_5F1_tree_canopy_plot-1.png){fig-alt='Line chart showing the percentage change in National Forest Inventory
woodland extent in the West of England from the 2020 baseline, covering
2020 to 2024. The y-axis shows percentage change on a scale from -1% to
+1%; the x-axis shows year. The line remains very close to zero
throughout, ending at approximately +0.3% by 2024, indicating a small
but positive increase in woodland cover since 2020.' width=672}
:::
